<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Accounting for computer scientists</title>
    <style>
body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 52em; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; line-height: 1.45; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1em 0; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #bbb; padding: 0.3em 0.7em; text-align: left; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
td.green { background: #d6f0d6; }
td.blue { background: #d6e6f8; }
td.pink { background: #f8d6e6; }
svg.graph { width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 1em 0; }
line.edge { stroke: #555; stroke-width: 1.5; marker-end: url(#arrow); }
polygon { fill: #555; }
circle.green { fill: #d6f0d6; stroke: #5a9a5a; stroke-width: 1.5; }
circle.blue { fill: #d6e6f8; stroke: #5a80b0; stroke-width: 1.5; }
circle.pink { fill: #f8d6e6; stroke: #b05a85; stroke-width: 1.5; }
text.label { text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: middle; font-size: 11px; }
text.amount { text-anchor: middle; font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; paint-order: stroke; stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 3px; }
table.statement { min-width: 22em; }
tr.total td { font-weight: bold; border-top: 2px solid #333; }
</style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Accounting for computer scientists</h1>
    <p>Basic accounting is graph theory. The company below is the example of Martin Kleppmann&#x27;s article of that name, worked out by a program.</p>
    <section>
      <h2>Accounts are nodes, transactions are edges</h2>
      <p>Each line is an edge of the graph: an amount flowing from one account to another. An account can be a bank account, a card, a customer, or an abstract category such as food or furniture. Accounts are coloured: green for what the company owns or owes, blue for revenue and expense, pink for the money its shareholders put in.</p>
      <svg class="graph" viewBox="0 0 780 390">
        <defs><marker id="arrow" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="9" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7"></polygon></marker></defs>
        <line class="edge" x1="480.0" y1="148.0" x2="480.0" y2="94.0"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="480.0" y="114.0">5.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="480.0" y1="232.0" x2="480.0" y2="286.0"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="480.0" y="254.0">500.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="522.0" y1="190.0" x2="656.0" y2="190.0"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="590.0" y="184.0">8,000.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="522.0" y1="50.0" x2="656.0" y2="50.0"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="590.0" y="44.0">13.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="522.0" y1="330.0" x2="656.0" y2="330.0"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="590.0" y="324.0">125.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="304.9" y1="73.3" x2="443.4" y2="165.6"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="375.0" y="114.0">5,000.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="312.0" y1="190.0" x2="436.0" y2="190.0"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="375.0" y="184.0">2,500.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="119.4" y1="105.5" x2="228.7" y2="65.2"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="175.0" y="79.0">5,000.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="119.4" y1="134.5" x2="228.7" y2="174.8"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="175.0" y="149.0">5,000.00</text>
        <line class="edge" x1="119.6" y1="316.1" x2="438.5" y2="204.5"></line>
        <text class="amount" x="280.0" y="254.0">25,000.00</text>
        <circle class="green" cx="480.0" cy="190.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="480.0" y="190.0">Bank account</text>
        <circle class="green" cx="480.0" cy="50.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="480.0" y="50.0">Credit card</text>
        <circle class="green" cx="480.0" cy="330.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="480.0" y="330.0">Furniture</text>
        <circle class="green" cx="270.0" cy="50.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="270.0" y="50.0">Customer 1</text>
        <circle class="green" cx="270.0" cy="190.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="270.0" y="190.0">Customer 2</text>
        <circle class="blue" cx="80.0" cy="120.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="80.0" y="120.0">Sales</text>
        <circle class="pink" cx="80.0" cy="330.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="80.0" y="330.0">Capital</text>
        <circle class="blue" cx="700.0" cy="190.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="700.0" y="190.0">Payroll</text>
        <circle class="blue" cx="700.0" cy="330.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="700.0" y="330.0">Depreciation</text>
        <circle class="blue" cx="700.0" cy="50.0" r="42"></circle>
        <text class="label" x="700.0" y="50.0">Food</text>
      </svg>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Transaction</th>
          <th>From</th>
          <th>To</th>
          <th>Amount</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A bagel on the company credit card</td>
          <td class="green">Credit card</td>
          <td class="blue">Food</td>
          <td class="num">5.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A chair, paid by cheque from the bank account</td>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="green">Furniture</td>
          <td class="num">500.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The founder puts in savings</td>
          <td class="pink">Capital</td>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="num">5,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The credit card bill is paid from the bank</td>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="green">Credit card</td>
          <td class="num">5.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A Super Burrito on the credit card</td>
          <td class="green">Credit card</td>
          <td class="blue">Food</td>
          <td class="num">8.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sale to customer 1, agreed at 5,000</td>
          <td class="blue">Sales</td>
          <td class="green">Customer 1</td>
          <td class="num">5,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sale to customer 2, agreed at 5,000</td>
          <td class="blue">Sales</td>
          <td class="green">Customer 2</td>
          <td class="num">5,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Customer 1 pays in full</td>
          <td class="green">Customer 1</td>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="num">5,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Customer 2 pays half up front</td>
          <td class="green">Customer 2</td>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="num">2,500.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Y Combinator invests</td>
          <td class="pink">Capital</td>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="num">20,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Salaries, paid from the bank</td>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="blue">Payroll</td>
          <td class="num">8,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The chair loses a quarter of its value to depreciation</td>
          <td class="green">Furniture</td>
          <td class="blue">Depreciation</td>
          <td class="num">125.00</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Balances</h2>
      <p>An account starts at zero. Money coming in adds to it, money going out subtracts. Every transaction is counted once as positive and once as negative, so all the balances add up to zero: that is what accountants call balancing the books.</p>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Account</th>
          <th>Balance</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="green">Bank account</td>
          <td class="num">23,995.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="green">Credit card</td>
          <td class="num">-8.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="green">Furniture</td>
          <td class="num">375.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="green">Customer 1</td>
          <td class="num">0.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="green">Customer 2</td>
          <td class="num">2,500.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="blue">Sales</td>
          <td class="num">-10,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="pink">Capital</td>
          <td class="num">-25,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="blue">Payroll</td>
          <td class="num">8,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="blue">Depreciation</td>
          <td class="num">125.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="blue">Food</td>
          <td class="num">13.00</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Profit and loss</h2>
      <p>Only the blue accounts: revenue less expenses. A negative balance on a blue account is revenue, so the sign flips when it is reported.</p>
      <table class="statement">
        <tr>
          <td>Revenue: sales</td>
          <td class="num">10,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Expenses: payroll</td>
          <td class="num">8,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Expenses: depreciation</td>
          <td class="num">125.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Expenses: food</td>
          <td class="num">13.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="total">
          <td>Profit</td>
          <td class="num">1,862.00</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Balance sheet</h2>
      <p>The green accounts on one side, the pink accounts and the profit on the other. Profit is not cash: the bank holds less than the 25,000 invested plus the sales, because customer 2 still owes half.</p>
      <table class="statement">
        <tr>
          <td>Assets: bank account</td>
          <td class="num">23,995.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Assets: debtors</td>
          <td class="num">2,500.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Assets: furniture</td>
          <td class="num">375.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Less liabilities: credit card</td>
          <td class="num">-8.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="total">
          <td>Assets less liabilities</td>
          <td class="num">26,862.00</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <table class="statement">
        <tr>
          <td>Equity: profit</td>
          <td class="num">1,862.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Equity: capital</td>
          <td class="num">25,000.00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="total">
          <td>Total equity</td>
          <td class="num">26,862.00</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>
  </body>
</html>
